  <version>2.0.1</version>
  <packaging>aar</packaging>
  <name>Scoop NFC SDK</name>
  <description>NFC SDK for reading German health cards (eGK) — a Kotlin Multiplatform library
enabling NFC-based smart card authentication using the PACE protocol.

The SDK provides:
• PACE protocol for NFC smart card authentication (eGK)
• Secure Messaging (SM) channel with automatic broken-channel detection and re-PACE
• eGK file system reading (VSD, PD, GDO)
• VSD XML parsing with insured person data extraction
• eGK card SVG visualization
• CAN scanning via CameraX + ML Kit text recognition
• APDU caching for improved performance
• Known-cards management
• Performance metrics and timing

Built with Kotlin Multiplatform (KMP), the SDK targets Android (this artifact)
and iOS (distributed as XCFramework via SPM). A Flutter binding is available
as the scoop_nfc package.</description>
  <url>https://github.com/scoop-software/nfc-sdk</url>
  <organization>
    <name>Scoop Software GmbH</name>
    <url>https://scoopsoftware.de</url>
